Z||000024||ChadMan||10-17-2001||11:09 AM||||I lost $10 on that damned game.  Corey Dillon is incredible.  Gloat while you can, BENGAL4.  It will be a different story on 11/25 when the Bungles come to Cleveland.<P>I feel your pain, Master Sushi.  To be honest, selling my 88 didn't hurt as bad as selling the 86 SE V6 I had.  With the 88, it was kind of like putting an old dog to sleep or breaking up with a high-school girlfriend who wants to have your kid...it hurts like hell but you've GOT to do it.  With the 86, I watched it pull away and heard those quad pipes burbling, then got in my 88 and fired up the Duke and I immediately knew I had just made one of the biggest mistakes of my life.<P>Still enjoying the Miata, though I can tell it is going to suck come wintertime.  If it ever stops raining long enough for me to wash it, I'll post a pic.<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000025||87ECO5||10-23-2001||01:55 PM||||I had an opportunity to hook up with Chad this past weekend and I got to drive the Miata.  This is a very nice car - as nice as I remember when I drove one back in 1989 (when they first debuted)!  The car handles wondefully, the exhaust note is classical, and that short-throw shifter is something we should all get to live with!!!  Unfortunately, I think my a$$ grew six inches wider since that first drive 'cause I felt somewhat cramped.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Good luck with it, Chad, and I hope we can stay in touch!||||reg||14
